==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{qualifier|as spelled}} {{IPA|/zː/|lang=en}}
* {{qualifier|imitation of snoring}} {{IPA|/ʩ/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|Zzz.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Supposed to represent the sound of snoring.

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# Implies that a particular character is [[asleep]].

===Verb===
{{en-verb|zzzs|zzzing|zzzed}}

# To [[sleep]].
#* H. G. Wells
#*: He lay back on his pillow, made a faint '''zzzing''' sound that ceased, and presently and quite quietly he died &mdash; greatly comforted by my assurance.
#* {{quote-book|year=1996|author=Charlotte Abrams|title=The Silents|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=H8I6MWc5MogC&pg=PA42&dq=zzzed&hl=en&sa=X&ei=YLcVUavPFKjfigL0lYCwBg&ved=0CDwQ6AEwAQ|page=42|passage=He '''zzzed''' for a long time, bobbing back and forth, and then he let us go, pointing to two empty seats across the aisle and motioning for us to sit down.}}

